# November 21, 2026: Chautauqua County, New York (the far western corner of the state): Westfield and Barcelona,
# Mayville, Chautauqua, Point Chautauqua, Maple Springs, Lily Dale, Brocton, Dunkirk, Silver Creek, Sherman, Clymer,
# Busti and Jamestown. Drawn at random by tools/choose.py --state ny (region wny, which offered Jamestown); the Atlas had
# no place within 40 km of Jamestown or Westfield. Mostly standing buildings: two lighthouses, four railroad buildings,
# two mills, a trolley park, three camp-meeting and resort communities, a museum village, a mansion museum, a truss
# bridge, a welcome arch, a land-office vault and a stone railroad arch. Sources opened in this session: Wikipedia as raw
# text (tools/wiki_raw.py, including the county Register list), and through tools/page.py the pages of NY State Parks,
# the Chautauqua Institution, the Fenton History Center, the Dunkirk Lighthouse museum, the Village of Sherman, HMdb
# markers, historypointer.com (Register addresses), the Post-Journal, the Villager, WRFA, Waymarking and the county
# tourism office (tourchautauqua.com). Every NPGallery Register form tried here was the one-page placeholder.
from data_b import N
from data_ma import W
def L(t,u): return [t,u]
BATCH={'key':'wny_rdxr','label':'Chautauqua County, NY: Westfield, Mayville, Chautauqua, Lily Dale, Dunkirk and Jamestown','added':'2026-11-21 03:29'}
REG=W('National Register of Historic Places listings in Chautauqua County, New York')
